WEBVTT

00:01.269 --> 00:04.910
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.977 --> 00:07.882
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.949 --> 00:11.189
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.255 --> 00:14.329
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.395 --> 00:18.136
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.236 --> 00:21.409
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:21.510 --> 00:23.113
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.146 --> 00:24.382
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.448 --> 00:30.360
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.101 --> 00:35.771
So, Brian's checkup
went very well.

00:35.872 --> 00:38.711
He only bit me eight times while
I tried to brush his teeth.

00:38.778 --> 00:41.784
Wonderful. And does he have
the red, hairless undercarriage

00:41.850 --> 00:43.588
-of an older dog?
-He sure does.

00:43.655 --> 00:46.159
He's the Jason Alexander
of hairless scroti.

00:46.226 --> 00:47.696
And you know,
if you're interested,

00:47.763 --> 00:49.431
we're doing a 50% off promotion

00:49.465 --> 00:51.402
on our new, state-of-the-art
tracking chip.

00:51.435 --> 00:54.308
It connects to an app
that will monitor Brian's vitals

00:54.375 --> 00:55.878
and even has a Bluetooth speaker

00:55.978 --> 00:57.280
so you can play songs
through him.

00:57.314 --> 00:59.151
Awesome! I'm gonna
blast Ed Sheeran

00:59.218 --> 01:00.220
right through his stomach.

01:00.320 --> 01:03.193
That'll really showcase
my milquetoast personality

01:03.259 --> 01:04.930
and lack of masculine vigor.

01:04.997 --> 01:06.166
Great. I'll introduce you
to our nurse

01:06.199 --> 01:07.134
who handles the procedure.

01:07.201 --> 01:08.670
Hi, I'm Emma.

01:08.737 --> 01:11.009
And don't worry, I'm wearing
scrubs that hide my tattoos

01:11.042 --> 01:12.078
to give you confidence.

01:12.178 --> 01:14.683
Terrific. And now, like
in every hospital situation,

01:14.749 --> 01:17.354
I'll depart and a woman
will do the actual work.

01:19.593 --> 01:21.329
Okay, we're almost done.

01:22.566 --> 01:24.168
And you're all set.

01:24.301 --> 01:25.571
[music playing faintly]

01:25.638 --> 01:27.876
[Peter] Yeah! Playin'
Ed Sheeran through my dog!

01:27.942 --> 01:29.212
I'm like a cool dentist!

01:29.279 --> 01:31.550
Wow, I barely felt that.
You're very gentle.

01:31.617 --> 01:33.654
[chuckles]
Thanks. I love animals.

01:33.754 --> 01:34.990
It's why I do this.

01:35.057 --> 01:38.229
I even pride myself on being
able to find every dog's spot,

01:38.329 --> 01:39.600
right behind the ears.

01:39.666 --> 01:41.870
Well, maybe you can
find mine sometime.

01:41.937 --> 01:43.273
I'd be tempted
to ask you to coffee,

01:43.340 --> 01:45.812
but I'm sure a girl like you
is already seeing someone.

01:45.912 --> 01:47.982
I wish. Guys don't want
a girlfriend

01:48.083 --> 01:49.953
who comes home
smelling like dog pee.

01:50.020 --> 01:51.289
I'm practically a fire hydrant.

01:51.356 --> 01:53.794
Is-is, uh, is, uh,
is that right?

01:53.861 --> 01:56.232
Yeah, and my car's so filthy.

01:56.332 --> 01:58.069
I need someone to stick
their head out the window

01:58.170 --> 01:59.171
to help navigate.

01:59.238 --> 02:00.407
H-Head-- head out the window?

02:00.508 --> 02:03.146
To be honest, all I like to do
is play tennis,

02:03.212 --> 02:04.649
but I'm not even that good.

02:04.683 --> 02:06.485
I keep hitting the balls
over the fence

02:06.553 --> 02:08.023
and have no one
to retrieve them--

02:08.090 --> 02:10.394
Hey, hey, babe? Babe? I'm in.

02:10.460 --> 02:13.133
Well, I'm going
to a concert this Friday.

02:13.200 --> 02:15.103
Want to come?
It's at Quahog Church.

02:15.170 --> 02:18.109
Church? So, is it, uh,
Christian rock?

02:18.176 --> 02:20.247
Yeah. I'm an evangelical
Christian.

02:20.314 --> 02:21.449
Is that a problem?

02:21.517 --> 02:23.253
Well, I-I'm not really
a big fan of--

02:23.320 --> 02:24.255
There's your spot.

02:24.321 --> 02:29.866
[announcer] ¡Gol!

02:34.108 --> 02:36.680
Sorry, I interrupted you.
You were saying?

02:36.747 --> 02:40.888
I-I-- why, just that I'm not a
big fan of anything, but Jesus!

02:40.955 --> 02:42.391
He's the best! [chuckles]

02:42.457 --> 02:44.730
Well, him and whoever
fired Bob Barker.

02:44.796 --> 02:45.998
Neuter yourself, dick.

02:46.065 --> 02:47.535
I know, what a jerk.

02:47.602 --> 02:49.840
Wasn't he also accused
of sexual harassment?

02:49.907 --> 02:50.975
Yeah, yeah, yeah...

02:51.075 --> 02:53.714
The dog stuff though,
you know, come on.

02:56.620 --> 02:59.526
[TV announcer] We now return to
The Italian Tony Awards.

02:59.626 --> 03:02.098
Hey, I'm Tony,
and for the 30th year in a row,

03:02.131 --> 03:05.237
the best musical is the only
one that I've seen, Cats.

03:05.270 --> 03:06.339
[audience member]
Hey, you hear that?

03:06.405 --> 03:07.976
Tony likes a musical.

03:08.043 --> 03:09.479
Eh, pipe down, boombots.

03:09.546 --> 03:11.951
Everybody knows in high school
you had an earring.

03:11.984 --> 03:13.821
All right, I'm going out.
I'll see you guys later.

03:13.887 --> 03:16.827
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
W-What's that around your neck?

03:18.463 --> 03:22.104
Well, I, uh, I may have
a date with a Christian girl.

03:22.171 --> 03:24.342
Huh. Must be hard
for you not to bite

03:24.442 --> 03:26.179
what's essentially
two crossed sticks.

03:26.312 --> 03:27.314
Oh, my God, it's so hard.

03:27.415 --> 03:28.684
It's literally
all I can think about.

03:28.751 --> 03:30.588
But I-I really
like this girl, you know?

03:30.688 --> 03:32.324
She's perfect
in every other way.

03:32.391 --> 03:33.528
I don't know, Bri.
You really think

03:33.595 --> 03:35.798
you can convince her
you're Christian?

03:37.602 --> 03:39.171
Oh, you're good.

03:39.238 --> 03:41.442
[band playing]

03:43.847 --> 03:48.190
Hello, evangelicals!
Who out there is boring?

03:48.256 --> 03:49.424
We are!

03:49.491 --> 03:51.630
That's right!
And before we start,

03:51.697 --> 03:53.233
I'd like to say a special hello

03:53.333 --> 03:55.303
to our only
Black audience member,

03:55.403 --> 03:56.606
who's in the front row,

03:56.707 --> 03:59.779
so he's caught
on all the camera shots.

04:01.583 --> 04:03.821
Wow. Look at all our diversity.

04:03.888 --> 04:06.459
Can you believe most people
think us evangelicals

04:06.526 --> 04:08.196
are a bunch of nerdy losers?

04:08.262 --> 04:09.867
No. Come on.

04:09.933 --> 04:11.302
Seriously, it's true.

04:11.369 --> 04:13.841
Hey, I-I don't normally do this,

04:13.907 --> 04:17.047
but what do you say we go back
to my place after this

04:17.147 --> 04:19.018
and get a little crazy?

04:19.118 --> 04:20.621
-Really?
-Yeah.

04:20.722 --> 04:24.161
We'll eat sherbet and watch
funny State Farm commercials.

04:24.262 --> 04:27.167
Uh, okay, and,
and then we'll have sex?

04:27.267 --> 04:29.438
Sex? Brian, I'm Christian.

04:29.505 --> 04:31.744
And no good Christian
believes in sex before marriage,

04:31.811 --> 04:34.381
except for every minister or
politician you've ever heard of.

04:34.481 --> 04:37.823
But-but you scratched my spot.
Y-You have tattoos.

04:37.889 --> 04:40.293
Yeah. Of Bible verses.

04:42.365 --> 04:44.503
[sighs] Brian, I think
you should leave.

04:44.569 --> 04:45.437
Well, fine. And frankly,

04:45.505 --> 04:47.474
I've been wanting
to do this all night.

04:48.243 --> 04:49.746
-My Jesus! Mine!
-[gasping]

04:49.813 --> 04:52.418
Hey, you can't do that
to our savior.

04:52.519 --> 04:56.058
-[growling]
-Okay, okay, your savior.
Your savior.

04:58.864 --> 05:01.335
[announcer]
We now return
to a show about incest.

05:01.435 --> 05:03.372
-Gross.
-Set 500 years ago.

05:03.406 --> 05:06.045
Ooh, sexy.
I feel so sophisticated.

05:06.145 --> 05:07.381
Christianity sucks.

05:07.481 --> 05:09.485
It's stupid, arbitrary nonsense.

05:09.553 --> 05:11.322
You're horny and she wouldn't
have sex with you.

05:11.389 --> 05:13.026
No. And I did everything right.

05:13.126 --> 05:14.529
I even researched
abortion clinics

05:14.596 --> 05:15.464
in case the condom broke.

05:15.598 --> 05:17.735
Yeah, no, I know.
It's in your Twitter bio.

05:21.442 --> 05:22.779
Fine, but look around.

05:22.845 --> 05:25.083
So much of the division
and hatred in today's society

05:25.183 --> 05:27.955
comes from Christianity.
And it's so hypocritical.

05:28.022 --> 05:30.293
I mean, they all vote for Trump,
even though he's divorced.

05:30.427 --> 05:31.429
That's all you've got on Trump?

05:31.495 --> 05:34.602
Christianity is also
anti-science, anti-freedom--

05:34.669 --> 05:36.138
Come on, it's not all bad.

05:36.238 --> 05:39.546
I mean, I have a Swarthy Men
of Nazareth advent calendar

05:39.646 --> 05:42.184
with doors opening
for all 25 days.

05:42.284 --> 05:44.923
Talk about the "stars"
of Bethlehem, hey, Bri?

05:44.989 --> 05:46.960
Whatever.
Christianity is the worst thing

05:47.027 --> 05:49.165
that ever happened
to this country. Or the world.

05:49.231 --> 05:51.570
Well, perhaps. But it's been
around for 2,000 years,

05:51.637 --> 05:53.941
so it's not like there's
anything you can do about it.

05:54.041 --> 05:55.076
Well, I'm going to bed.

05:55.176 --> 05:56.446
I'll leave you
to watch John Oliver

05:56.513 --> 05:57.782
and agree with yourself.

05:57.882 --> 06:00.988
Good. Love John Oliver.
He's a louder Jon Stewart.

06:01.055 --> 06:05.063
[John Oliver]
Blimey, guv'na.
Republicans are bollocks.

06:05.096 --> 06:06.633
God, the British are smart.

06:06.733 --> 06:09.471
But, man, if only
I could get rid of Christianity.

06:09.539 --> 06:10.741
If only I could go back in time

06:10.808 --> 06:13.046
and stop it
from ever taking root.

06:13.112 --> 06:14.916
Wait a minute, I can.

06:14.983 --> 06:16.285
[thunder crashing]

06:16.352 --> 06:17.722
[West]
Sounds like Brian is fixin'

06:17.789 --> 06:19.726
to use Stewie's time machine.

06:19.826 --> 06:21.495
[sped up]
I'm Mayor West,
and my voice was sped up

06:21.563 --> 06:23.399
because the show ran too long.

06:35.725 --> 06:37.060
[beeps]

06:37.127 --> 06:39.365
[computer voice]
This time machine
is password-protected.

06:39.431 --> 06:41.136
To enter, state name.

06:41.202 --> 06:43.205
Uh, uh, Stewie Griffin.

06:43.305 --> 06:45.143
To prove you're Stewie Griffin,

06:45.210 --> 06:47.047
what is your
favorite Lizzo song?

06:47.081 --> 06:50.187
Uh, the one about pride and, uh,

06:50.253 --> 06:52.525
being a... a-a big girl?

06:52.625 --> 06:53.927
-Correct.
-[chimes]

06:55.898 --> 06:58.069
[beeping rapidly]

07:14.603 --> 07:16.506
Perfect. Ancient Israel.

07:16.573 --> 07:18.511
♪ And I know my worth... ♪

07:18.611 --> 07:19.879
What the hell?

07:19.979 --> 07:21.149
Has anyone seen Brian?

07:21.215 --> 07:22.685
I want to shred it to Lizzo.

07:22.785 --> 07:24.388
Oh, yeah, I'm that bitch.

07:24.488 --> 07:26.994
-♪ Am I ready? ♪
-♪ Ready to go ♪

07:27.061 --> 07:28.095
♪ Am I ready? ♪

07:35.978 --> 07:38.584
Uh, excuse me? I-I'm looking
for a rail-thin guy

07:38.650 --> 07:40.420
with long hair and sandals.

07:40.487 --> 07:42.926
Buddy, you're gonna have
to be more specific.

07:42.993 --> 07:45.363
Uh, his name is Jesus.
Jesus Christ.

07:45.430 --> 07:48.504
You mean the guy who showed
his wiener on a dare at camp?

07:48.571 --> 07:50.473
Tha-That's-that's
what he's known for?

07:50.541 --> 07:53.379
Yeah, he lives about
M-M-L-X-V-I paces that way.

07:53.413 --> 07:54.749
-What?
-Don't listen to him.

07:54.849 --> 07:58.055
He's Roman. I'm Egyptian,
and I can tell you,

07:58.122 --> 08:02.263
Jesus lives four cat heads and
three squiggly lines that way.

08:02.330 --> 08:03.901
No, no, no,
these guys are jokers.

08:04.001 --> 08:07.141
I'm Greek, and I can tell you
he's 30 thetas that way.

08:07.207 --> 08:08.877
You go 31 thetas, you stop,

08:08.944 --> 08:11.115
because that's too many thetas.

08:12.685 --> 08:14.454
-Brian, there you are.
-Stewie?

08:14.522 --> 08:16.626
-How the hell did you find me?
-You're chipped.

08:18.129 --> 08:19.231
Wow, that's a good chip.

08:19.297 --> 08:21.736
Look, I'm sorry I used
the time machine without asking,

08:21.837 --> 08:24.709
but I came here to stop Jesus
from starting Christianity.

08:24.809 --> 08:26.445
What? Come on,
you know the rules.

08:26.513 --> 08:27.716
You can't change the past.

08:27.816 --> 08:29.719
Even the smallest interaction
with someone

08:29.786 --> 08:31.255
from another time period
can alter--

08:31.289 --> 08:34.227
Oh, my God, that's December 8th
from the calendar!

08:34.327 --> 08:35.263
I have to interact with him.

08:35.363 --> 08:37.133
I thought you said
we couldn't change the past.

08:37.167 --> 08:38.771
Uh, yeah, just try to keep it
close, all right?

08:38.838 --> 08:40.741
Just keep it close, Bri.
You got this.

08:40.808 --> 08:42.645
You got this. I trust you, bro.

08:46.719 --> 08:49.525
"Spicy meatball
delights patron."

08:49.659 --> 08:52.565
Ugh, no one reports
real news anymore.

08:53.767 --> 08:55.470
All right, found you.

08:55.538 --> 08:58.008
Now it's time to take you down.

09:00.648 --> 09:02.819
Behold. As my wedding gift,

09:02.885 --> 09:05.958
I turn this water into wine.

09:06.025 --> 09:07.595
[cheering]

09:07.628 --> 09:09.197
-All right!
-Amazing!

09:09.264 --> 09:11.837
And I brought hard seltzer
and a photo booth.

09:11.937 --> 09:13.607
-[cheering]
-Yeah, that's even better!

09:13.674 --> 09:15.210
Hard seltzer has less calories.

09:15.243 --> 09:18.082
And now there's an activity for
people who don't like to dance.

09:18.182 --> 09:21.923
Then, uh, I-I also brought
a guest book,

09:21.990 --> 09:24.328
so everyone can leave a fun note

09:24.394 --> 09:26.064
for the bride and groom.

09:27.568 --> 09:30.139
Okay, fine, a photo booth
is better.

09:36.251 --> 09:38.591
Blessed are the poor in spirit,

09:38.691 --> 09:40.528
for theirs is the kingdom
of heaven--

09:40.594 --> 09:41.530
[Brian]
Hey, Jesus.

09:41.596 --> 09:43.232
Nice mount.

09:43.299 --> 09:45.838
He's on a higher hill,
which shows more confidence.

09:45.938 --> 09:48.544
You again?
What the hell is your problem?

09:48.611 --> 09:49.979
Me? What the hell
is your problem?

09:50.112 --> 09:52.483
You're always telling everyone
what to do and think.

09:52.551 --> 09:54.021
You think I want
to do this stuff?

09:54.121 --> 09:56.560
I only do it because
my dad makes me.

09:56.627 --> 09:58.329
Wait, Joseph makes you do this?

09:58.429 --> 09:59.899
No, my real dad.

09:59.999 --> 10:02.705
When I was younger,
Joseph took a paternity test.

10:02.839 --> 10:06.179
We have the results,
and, Joseph,

10:06.245 --> 10:07.915
you are not the father.

10:07.982 --> 10:11.489
Yes! Yes! Yes!
I knew it! I knew it!

10:11.556 --> 10:14.929
[audience]
Maury! Maury! Maury!

10:18.904 --> 10:22.812
So, anyway, yeah, all this
messiah stuff is my dad's thing.

10:22.879 --> 10:25.617
Hi, I have a hummus plate
for Jesus?

10:25.684 --> 10:27.120
Oh, cool.

10:27.187 --> 10:29.859
Okay, I guess it's
for both of us.

10:29.959 --> 10:32.598
Well, if you don't want to be a
messiah, what do you want to do?

10:32.632 --> 10:35.036
Honestly, I want to be
a stand-up comedian.

10:35.103 --> 10:38.143
-Really?
-Yeah. Like my friend
Jackie the Mason

10:38.209 --> 10:41.248
or Lewis the Blacksmith
or Chris the Rock-Piler.

10:41.315 --> 10:44.187
You know, we can ask
for another menu if--

10:44.254 --> 10:45.691
Yeah, I'm not that hungry.

10:45.791 --> 10:47.862
So, why didn't you
do comedy, then?

10:47.929 --> 10:49.465
I guess I never had
the confidence.

10:49.533 --> 10:51.035
I couldn't even
come up with jokes.

10:51.135 --> 10:54.976
-[sneezes]
-Yikes. Check out
Julius Sneezer over there.

10:55.076 --> 10:56.045
Ha! Totally.

10:56.145 --> 10:57.447
Hey, you know,
that's pretty funny.

10:57.548 --> 10:59.217
What was? That comment?

10:59.317 --> 11:00.220
[farts]

11:00.320 --> 11:02.157
Whoa. Who Sepharted?

11:02.257 --> 11:05.230
Ha! Hey, you know, I think you
should give comedy another shot.

11:05.330 --> 11:07.868
Come on, does anyone really
want to watch a Jewish guy

11:07.935 --> 11:09.873
make snarky observations?

11:09.973 --> 11:13.112
I-I think, uh, that a lot
of people would enjoy that, yes.

11:13.179 --> 11:15.885
Huh. Then maybe I should
try comedy again.

11:16.018 --> 11:18.723
Only thing is, I'd have
to talk to my dad.

11:22.932 --> 11:24.401
♪ ♪

11:24.468 --> 11:27.241
Wow, I went to a party
in this city called Sodom.

11:27.307 --> 11:29.579
Have you heard of this place?
[whistles]

11:29.646 --> 11:30.814
So, how's your plan going?

11:30.914 --> 11:32.518
Uh, not great so far.

11:32.584 --> 11:33.754
A comedian?

11:33.821 --> 11:35.256
How could you do this
to your mother?

11:35.356 --> 11:36.325
-[sobbing]
-What's next?

11:36.458 --> 11:38.697
You don't want to marry
your very close cousin?

11:38.797 --> 11:40.499
Of course not.
In fact, right now

11:40.567 --> 11:43.674
I'm weirdly seeing a prostitute
with the same name as Mom.

11:43.774 --> 11:45.176
[sobbing]

11:45.276 --> 11:47.749
Come on, Dad,
comedy is my dream.

11:47.815 --> 11:49.753
Well, why couldn't you have
told me about your dream

11:49.820 --> 11:51.656
before I paid
for ancient Brandeis?

11:51.689 --> 11:52.725
You made me go there.

11:52.791 --> 11:55.230
You know, nothing I do
is ever good enough for you.

11:55.330 --> 11:57.201
Why don't you just say it?
You hate me.

11:57.267 --> 11:59.437
And you wish I had died
in the Punic Wars

11:59.538 --> 12:01.241
instead of my brother Greg.

12:02.143 --> 12:04.515
That's not true!
I love you both equally!

12:04.582 --> 12:05.851
Then why won't you
touch his room?

12:05.951 --> 12:07.387
You stay out of Greg's room!

12:07.453 --> 12:08.824
I have to do something.

12:08.891 --> 12:11.295
It's God. How could you
possibly change his mind?

12:11.362 --> 12:13.867
You will never do
stand-up comedy. I forbid it.

12:13.934 --> 12:15.270
["Danny's Song"
by Loggins and Messina playing]

12:15.336 --> 12:17.174
Wait. What's that sound?

12:17.240 --> 12:21.950
♪ People smile and tell me
I'm the lucky one ♪

12:22.017 --> 12:25.925
♪ And we've just begun ♪

12:25.991 --> 12:28.095
♪ Think I'm gonna
have a son... ♪

12:28.229 --> 12:29.933
That's really good
sound quality.

12:30.000 --> 12:32.203
-Yeah, it's the new iPhone.
-You got a new one?

12:32.270 --> 12:35.243
We agreed to update at the end
of the year, as Christmas gifts.

12:35.310 --> 12:37.280
Well, I was in the mall
and I saw a promotion.

12:37.380 --> 12:39.018
You didn't tell me
about this promotion.

12:39.084 --> 12:40.787
Oh, I-I'm sorry, I didn't
realize I had to tell you

12:40.854 --> 12:42.692
every [bleep] thought
that comes into my head.

12:42.758 --> 12:44.863
Okay, there we go,
Brian makes a mistake,

12:44.996 --> 12:47.735
so instead of apologizing,
he lashes out with hostility.

12:47.802 --> 12:50.006
And Stewie's a victim.
There's a big surprise.

12:50.106 --> 12:52.411
I'm a victim because
you constantly screw me over.

12:52.545 --> 12:54.883
You know what? Now I wish
I hadn't even played this song.

12:54.950 --> 12:56.586
I wish I hadn't
even come back in time.

12:56.719 --> 12:57.755
Because I can't do anything

12:57.822 --> 12:59.491
without you making it
about yourself.

12:59.626 --> 13:00.861
God, I regret our friendship.

13:00.928 --> 13:02.330
You are a catastrophe
of a human.

13:02.430 --> 13:03.867
Oh, hey, they made up.

13:03.900 --> 13:10.346
♪ Tell me everything's
gonna be all right. ♪

13:14.789 --> 13:17.861
[trumpets blaring]

13:22.370 --> 13:24.341
Well, it's great
to be here in Rome, folks.

13:24.408 --> 13:27.047
Uh, you know, I heard
that the, uh, Roman Senate

13:27.113 --> 13:29.852
just voted to build
more cobblestone streets.

13:29.919 --> 13:32.490
Great. Do my balls get a vote?

13:32.591 --> 13:34.127
[laughter]

13:34.161 --> 13:37.568
And how about that Caesar, huh?
Gotta love Caesar.

13:37.634 --> 13:39.171
Great salad, great haircut,

13:39.271 --> 13:41.776
and loves cutting
women's bellies open.

13:41.843 --> 13:42.778
[laughter]

13:42.845 --> 13:44.849
Look at him there,
in the Caesarian section.

13:44.949 --> 13:46.385
They're laughing their ass off.

13:46.451 --> 13:48.222
I do. I do love that.

13:48.356 --> 13:50.360
And you know what they say,
"When in Rome."

13:50.427 --> 13:53.232
Well, based on my
one day here so far,

13:53.298 --> 13:56.773
I guess that means I should be
pooping in the street.

13:56.840 --> 13:59.445
He's right.
That is a problem here.

13:59.512 --> 14:02.785
But seriously, folks,
Rome sure beats anywhere else.

14:02.885 --> 14:04.221
You guys follow politics?

14:04.321 --> 14:07.193
'Cause it seems like they've
made a real mess of Potamia.

14:07.293 --> 14:09.832
[laughter]

14:09.965 --> 14:13.072
But don't fret, folks,
it's not all bad news out there.

14:13.139 --> 14:15.410
You know how there are
seven wonders of the world?

14:15.477 --> 14:17.147
Well, turns out
they just found an eighth.

14:17.214 --> 14:20.086
A Galatian who paid his bar tab.

14:20.119 --> 14:21.956
-[laughter]
-Galatia is our rival.

14:22.023 --> 14:23.727
But enough about politics.

14:23.827 --> 14:25.864
Let me tell you
a little bit about me.

14:25.965 --> 14:28.269
So, my dad's God.

14:28.369 --> 14:29.070
[crowd cheering]

14:29.170 --> 14:30.574
Thank you, thank you.

14:30.641 --> 14:33.813
And growing up, he taught me
all about carpentry. Yeah.

14:33.880 --> 14:35.784
Uh, I guess
he thought teenage boys

14:35.851 --> 14:38.657
should spend more time
rubbing wood.

14:38.724 --> 14:39.893
[crowd laughs]

14:39.959 --> 14:42.030
And my mom's a virgin.

14:42.130 --> 14:43.398
That's fun. Uh, yeah,

14:43.432 --> 14:46.338
when I was a teenager,
I had to give her the talk.

14:46.438 --> 14:47.641
[crowd laughs]

14:49.646 --> 14:52.050
[cheering]

14:52.150 --> 14:53.385
Wow, he's killing it.

14:53.452 --> 14:55.356
Yeah, I bet
he plays everywhere now.

14:55.423 --> 14:56.559
He's gonna be huge.

15:00.300 --> 15:01.936
-What happened?
-He told a joke

15:02.037 --> 15:04.007
about Assyrians
on a college campus.

15:04.074 --> 15:05.342
Oh, yeah, you can't
do that anymore.

15:05.442 --> 15:08.015
This first millennial
generation is very sensitive.

15:08.115 --> 15:09.919
-Clearly.
-All right,
don't make it obvious,

15:09.986 --> 15:12.123
but get a picture of me
with him.

15:12.925 --> 15:14.595
-Do one more.
-Stewie, we're done.

15:14.662 --> 15:16.633
Mission accomplished and
Christianity never happened,

15:16.700 --> 15:19.739
so I'm pretty sure the present
will be just how I want it.

15:19.772 --> 15:21.074
[Peter]
Hi, Peter here.

15:21.174 --> 15:23.245
If you've seen our
time travel episodes before,

15:23.312 --> 15:24.982
you know that can't
possibly be the case.

15:25.082 --> 15:27.320
I can't tell you
what's going to happen, though,

15:27.387 --> 15:29.024
because the network
needs you to stick around

15:29.090 --> 15:30.092
through the Del Taco ads.

15:30.159 --> 15:31.696
You know, if you bought
all the ingredients

15:31.829 --> 15:34.201
for tacos yourself,
it would cost like 40 bucks,

15:34.268 --> 15:37.273
but somehow, at Del Taco,
you can buy one for 80 cents.

15:54.809 --> 15:56.178
-Damn it.
-What? What's wrong?

15:56.278 --> 15:58.182
Every time I enter
into a new reality,

15:58.316 --> 16:00.086
I'm hoping
my room has wainscoting.

16:00.220 --> 16:02.056
[sighs]
But I guess it's more boring,

16:02.123 --> 16:04.427
single-textured walls
for Stewie.

16:06.900 --> 16:08.937
Wow, so far,
without Christianity,

16:09.070 --> 16:10.541
everything looks the same.

16:11.342 --> 16:13.547
Morning, Brian.
Hey, where's your yarmulke?

16:13.647 --> 16:14.782
Uh, what?

16:14.849 --> 16:16.051
Morning, Doctor Son.

16:16.118 --> 16:17.688
Morning, Doctor Dad.

16:17.788 --> 16:18.957
Morning, Doctor Wife.

16:19.023 --> 16:20.594
Morning, Doctor Husband.

16:20.661 --> 16:22.296
Oh, my God. They're all Jewish.

16:22.363 --> 16:24.969
Whoa. Listen to your tone.

16:25.069 --> 16:26.404
No, no, no. No tone at all.

16:26.506 --> 16:28.308
Because Christianity
never happened,

16:28.375 --> 16:29.979
Judaism became
the dominant faith,

16:30.046 --> 16:31.817
and I have
zero problem with that.

16:31.883 --> 16:33.052
Why, do you have a problem?

16:33.118 --> 16:34.956
No, I don't have a problem.
Far from it.

16:35.023 --> 16:37.595
What the yidle-diddle-diddle-
didle-deuce?

16:37.661 --> 16:41.435
Well, I'm off to school
in my regular-star necklace.

16:41.503 --> 16:42.404
I'm leaving, too.

16:42.470 --> 16:44.642
Mom, Dad,
I need some new clothes.

16:44.708 --> 16:45.577
Is it okay if I stop at

16:45.710 --> 16:47.948
Ross Dress for the Same Price as
Everywhere Else?

16:48.015 --> 16:49.952
Of course, honey.
Ooh, and maybe tonight

16:50.085 --> 16:52.123
we can all go see
that new movie starring

16:52.223 --> 16:55.330
Adam Sandler, Ben Stiller
and half of Scarlett Johansson.

16:55.396 --> 16:57.835
Huh. So, you think
everyone is Jewish now?

16:57.968 --> 17:00.173
Morning, Griffins.
It's me, your neighbor,

17:00.239 --> 17:02.444
Sammy Davis Brown Jr.

17:02.545 --> 17:03.513
I suppose so.

17:03.613 --> 17:06.051
Wow, I guess a lot of
history has changed now.

17:06.117 --> 17:08.389
No World War II,
no conflict in the Middle East.

17:08.456 --> 17:10.259
Hell, there was even
a Jewish Columbus.

17:10.359 --> 17:13.566
We did it.
We discovered New York, Miami,

17:13.666 --> 17:14.936
and Filene's Basement.

17:15.003 --> 17:16.105
[all]
Yay!

17:16.171 --> 17:18.543
[chanting]
Slacks, slacks, slacks, slacks!

17:22.584 --> 17:24.655
Lot more sweater shops
in this reality.

17:24.755 --> 17:27.728
Yeah, and there's a billboard
for The Normal Mrs. Maisel.

17:27.795 --> 17:29.330
Ah, here we are.

17:33.539 --> 17:35.376
Shalom, Brian.

17:35.410 --> 17:38.182
Boy, this town has
good medical care.

17:38.249 --> 17:39.919
Are you sure
I'm allowed to be in here?

17:39.985 --> 17:41.288
Yeah, without Christianity,

17:41.355 --> 17:43.425
there are no arbitrary rules
about age limits.

17:43.492 --> 17:45.196
Hey, you guys hear the new joke?

17:45.229 --> 17:47.935
A rabbi, a rabbi,
and a rabbi walk into a bar

17:48.002 --> 17:49.605
and split a seltzer.

17:49.706 --> 17:51.474
It's free refills.

17:51.576 --> 17:53.980
Why pay for three?

17:54.782 --> 17:57.020
All right, what does everyone
want to hear on the jukebox?

17:57.087 --> 17:58.656
They've got "Sweet Caroline,"

17:58.756 --> 17:59.926
"Sweet Caroline Remix,"

18:00.026 --> 18:01.829
and "Sweet Caroline
A Cappella."

18:01.896 --> 18:03.634
Shalom, boys.

18:03.700 --> 18:05.570
Uh, shalom. How are you?

18:05.604 --> 18:08.009
Not good.
I'm allergic to my horse.

18:08.075 --> 18:09.344
Hey, Bri, I got the remote.

18:09.444 --> 18:11.014
Let's see
what television is like.

18:11.114 --> 18:13.118
[TV announcer]
And now, the Channel Five News,

18:13.218 --> 18:15.691
brought to you by
Kentucky Boiled Chicken.

18:15.791 --> 18:17.359
Kentucky Boiled Chicken:

18:17.393 --> 18:20.433
all herbs, no spices
'cause you already burp enough.

18:20.500 --> 18:22.003
Good afternoon, I'm Tom Tucker

18:22.103 --> 18:23.439
and welcome to Channel Five,

18:23.540 --> 18:26.679
where, as always,
80% of our news is the weather.

18:26.746 --> 18:29.184
But first, with sports,
here's my brother Lenny,

18:29.251 --> 18:30.954
who my mom forced me to hire.

18:31.021 --> 18:32.190
I-I'm sorry, Tom,

18:32.257 --> 18:33.593
I didn't have time
to check the scores.

18:33.660 --> 18:36.431
Well, there's
a friggin' shocker, folks.

18:40.305 --> 18:41.709
[in deep voice]
Afternoon, Brian.

18:41.742 --> 18:44.314
Hey, Mort.
Uh, why is your voice so deep?

18:44.381 --> 18:45.583
Why shouldn't it be?

18:45.650 --> 18:47.253
Millennia of
not running from people

18:47.353 --> 18:50.026
has made me remarkably
confident and relaxed.

18:50.093 --> 18:52.063
You know, I like Jewish Quahog.

18:52.163 --> 18:53.498
Yeah, we did
a good thing, Stewie.

18:53.599 --> 18:55.938
A Jewish world is much better
than a Christian one.

18:56.038 --> 18:59.545
There are no absurd, stifling
rules driving everyone crazy.

19:00.614 --> 19:01.616
There you guys are.

19:01.749 --> 19:04.454
It's almost sundown,
so let's turn off our devices

19:04.522 --> 19:06.859
-and walk three miles to temple.
-What?

19:06.959 --> 19:09.330
Ha! You were saying, Brian?

19:09.999 --> 19:11.034
We have to go back in time

19:11.134 --> 19:13.773
and stop Moses from receiving
the Ten Commandments.

19:13.840 --> 19:17.446
That way, neither Judaism nor
Christianity will ever exist.

19:17.547 --> 19:18.683
On it.

19:20.185 --> 19:22.123
-Done.
-How'd you do that so fast?

19:22.224 --> 19:24.261
I gave Moses 20 bucks
to walk away.

19:24.394 --> 19:25.530
And before you say anything,

19:25.597 --> 19:26.999
that was
a lot of money back then.

19:27.066 --> 19:28.569
Anyone would have done it.

19:32.377 --> 19:34.280
Happy November 25th.

19:34.381 --> 19:36.953
Only 30 shopping days
till nothing.

19:37.020 --> 19:38.221
Brian, it worked.

19:38.288 --> 19:39.592
That's only
half the story, Stewie.

19:39.659 --> 19:40.827
Let's make sure.

19:41.529 --> 19:43.766
Hey, guys?
Who does Mel Gibson hate?

19:43.833 --> 19:46.639
Uh, all of his ex-wives,
but no generalized group.

19:46.739 --> 19:48.710
It did work.
Finally, a world with

19:48.810 --> 19:52.283
no religion, no prejudices,
no irrationalities.

19:52.383 --> 19:54.788
-Just science-based reason.
-[knock on door]

19:55.890 --> 19:57.160
Package for Brian and Stewie?

19:57.260 --> 19:58.630
Yeah, that's us.

19:58.730 --> 20:00.701
What did you do,
you little twerps?

20:00.801 --> 20:01.936
Oh, my God. God!

20:02.003 --> 20:02.838
Fix it. Fix it.

20:03.005 --> 20:04.441
-Fix it. Fix it. Fix it. Fix it.
-Ow, ow, ow, ow!

20:04.509 --> 20:05.844
It was his idea!
It's not even my machine!

20:05.944 --> 20:08.683
You don't think Einstein
and Carl Sagan tried this crap?

20:08.750 --> 20:10.453
I had to send
them to Noogie City.

20:10.521 --> 20:11.388
Is that where you want to live?

20:11.523 --> 20:13.694
Noogie City? Huh?
'Cause I can take you there.

20:13.760 --> 20:14.895
I got the keys, hoss.

20:14.962 --> 20:16.331
[both grunting]

20:16.431 --> 20:17.901
Is this all religion is?

20:18.001 --> 20:19.337
Threatening to noogie people

20:19.404 --> 20:20.707
if they dare to think
for themselves?

20:20.774 --> 20:23.211
Yes. I'm basically Biff
from Back to the Future,

20:23.311 --> 20:24.581
and you're all George McFly.

20:24.648 --> 20:26.351
All right, I got to take
a picture of the package

20:26.451 --> 20:28.188
on your doorstep,
or they don't believe me.

20:28.255 --> 20:29.525
You're really a delivery man?

20:29.592 --> 20:31.227
Yeah. No collection plate.

20:31.294 --> 20:33.098
I got to pay for
Dish Network somehow.

20:33.198 --> 20:35.202
Oh, boy, we really
messed with this guy.

20:35.303 --> 20:36.939
I guess we should
go fix it, Brian.

20:37.040 --> 20:38.175
You know what? No.

20:38.275 --> 20:40.680
A world without religion
is a world that values

20:40.747 --> 20:43.251
reason and logic to better
the world for everyone.

20:43.318 --> 20:45.189
And I'm not gonna
let some two-bit boomer--

20:45.289 --> 20:47.126
yeah, you heard me--
tell us otherwise.

20:47.193 --> 20:49.063
[knuckles crack]

20:49.130 --> 20:53.940
♪ Christ the royal master ♪

20:54.040 --> 20:58.281
♪ Leads against the foe. ♪